        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "The turning point is $(2,21)$, so the maximum height is $21\\text{ m}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "When is the ball at its maximum height?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\text{ s}$",
          "worked": "The turning point occurs at $t=2$, so the ball reaches its maximum height after $2\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "At which two times is the ball 16 m above the ground?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\text{ s}$ and $3\\text{ s}$",
          "worked": "The horizontal line $h=16$ meets the curve at $t=1$ and $t=3$. The ball is $16\\text{ m}$ high after $1\\text{ s}$ and $3\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "At approximately what time is the height zero? Give your answer to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4.05\\text{ s}$",
          "worked": "The positive horizontal intercept is just after $t=4$. The ball reaches the ground at approximately $4.05\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "What is the value of $h$ when $t=5$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-24\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}h&=-5(5)^2+20(5)+1\\\\h&=-125+100+1\\\\h&=-24\\text{ m}\\end{aligned}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "What limitations are there on this model?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "From launch until the ball hits the ground, approximately $0\\leq t\\leq4.05$ seconds; time and height must be nonnegative.",
          "worked": "The model applies from launch until the positive horizontal intercept, approximately $4.05\\text{ s}$. Time cannot be negative and the ball cannot go below ground. The exact domain is $0\\leq t\\leq2+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{105}}5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
